use flake

# Export the credentials (git-ignored `.env.secrets`, written by `make env-pull`) plus the
# non-secret compose values in `.env` into the shell, so tools that read from the environment (e.g.
# the Neon and Grafana MCP servers) can see them. Keep secrets in `.env.secrets`, NOT here —
# .envrc itself IS tracked by git.
dotenv_if_exists .env
dotenv_if_exists .env.secrets
